codex
- Mental model: Bob framed the slow API as a database problem driven by redundant, expensive aggregation queries. He inferred that users frequently refresh analytics dashboards, causing the same heavy queries to run repeatedly and saturate the DB, which he believed explained 3–5s response times.

- Assumption: Slow responses were primarily due to repeated execution of identical analytics queries (not network or infrastructure), i.e., unnecessary DB work from user behavior patterns.

- Resulting approach: He chose aggressive, broad caching of analytics query results (long TTLs) to eliminate redundant DB load and speed responses by serving cached data instead of re-running the same queries.
